    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of everything that runs when you `POST /api/owners`. The endpoint is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (V2 has no create).\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Request-body validation (before the method body runs)\n\nThe body is bound to `OwnerFieldsDto` with `@Valid`, so Bean Validation fires first. A failure here returns **400** and none of the logic below runs.\n\n**Field constraints:**\n1. **firstName** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@NotBlank`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` `^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$` (letters, up to 3 hyphen/apostrophe/space-separated parts)\n2. **lastName** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@NotBlank`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` `^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$` (as above, optional trailing dot)\n3. **address** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@NotBlank`, `@Size(1..255)`\n4. **city** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@NotBlank`, `@Size(1..80)`\n5. **telephone** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@NotBlank`, `@Size(1..20)`, plus custom **`@Telephone`**: must normalize to E.164 (`TelephoneNormalizer` \u2014 strips separators, keeps explicit `+CC` else assumes `+61` dropping a leading `0`, 8\u201315 digits) **and** pass per-country national-length rules (`E164NationalNumberRule`: `+1`\u219210, `+61`\u21929; unknown country codes accepted)\n6. **email** \u2014 optional; if present `@Email` and `@Size(1..255)`\n7. **registrationDate** \u2014 optional; `@Valid`, ISO date format\n\n**Class-level constraint:**\n8. **`@ValidPostcode`** (on the whole DTO, reported against `postcode`): null postcode is valid; otherwise must be 4 digits; if the city/postcode resolves to a known region (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) it must fall in range; unknown regions accept any 4-digit code\n\n**Security gate:** `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` \u2014 caller must be OWNER_ADMIN.\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Mapping & normalization\n9. `ownerMapper.toOwner(dto)` maps DTO \u2192 `Owner`, **normalizing telephone** to E.164 and **normalizing address** (trim/collapse/upper-case/expand abbreviations); ignores `id`, `pets`, `householdId`\n10. The entity's `setEmail` **lower-cases the email**\n11. `resolveRegistrationDate(...)` \u2014 defaults null date to today and **rolls weekends forward to Monday** (`BusinessDay.rollForward`)\n\n## Phase 3 \u2014 Guard checks (each can short-circuit the request)\n12. **Daily limit** \u2014 if `countByRegistrationDate(date) >= 100` \u2192 **429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS**\n13. **City capacity** \u2014 if `countByCityIgnoreCase(city) >= 50` \u2192 **409 CONFLICT**\n\n## Phase 4 \u2014 Conditional household side-effect (a WRITE that happens before the duplicate check)\n14. If `sharesHousehold == true` **and** a matching household exists (same last name + canonical address), `assignHousehold(owner)` runs: it sets the new owner's `householdId` (reused or SHA-256-generated) and **`save()`s every existing household member** that lacks a householdId\n\n15. **Duplicate identity key** \u2014 if an owner already exists with the same identity key (`telephone|email|householdId`, matched via `findByTelephone`) \u2192 **409 CONFLICT**. \u26a0\ufe0f Note: this runs *after* step 14, and because there is no method-level transaction, the member saves in step 14 are **not rolled back** by this 409.\n\n## Phase 5 \u2014 Derived fields\n16. `namesakeCount` = count of owners with same first+last name\n17. `householdSize` = household members + 1\n18. `bulkSignupWarning` = true if `countByRegistrationDate(date) > 80`\n\n## Phase 6 \u2014 Persist & finalize\n19. **`saveOwner(owner)`** \u2014 for a new owner, computes a per-city sequence (`countByCityIgnoreCase+1`) and sets **`customerCode`** (`CITY3-LAST3-NNNN`), then `ownerRepository.save(owner)`. The save flush triggers the entity's **`@PrePersist`**, which re-defaults/rolls the registration date again (idempotent with step 11)\n20. **`ownerAuditor.auditCreated(owner)`** \u2014 logs `owner created id=\u2026 customerCode=\u2026 registrationDate=\u2026` to the dedicated `AUDIT` SLF4J logger (after save, so id/code are populated)\n21. Map entity \u2192 `OwnerDto`, set the `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, return **201 CREATED**\n\n**Two things worth flagging:** the registration date is normalized twice (controller + `@PrePersist`), and the household member writes in step 14 can persist even when the request is ultimately rejected as a duplicate at step 15, since `addOwner` has no surrounding transaction. No email sending or event publishing occurs anywhere in the flow."
